WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.640
Fictional heartbreak matching reality, fighting&nbsp;
for Raj's character, and huge celebrity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:09.548
what-ifs. These are the most eye-opening&nbsp;
things from 'The Big Bang Theory' book.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:14.340
There's a solid case to be made that "The Big&nbsp;
Bang Theory" wouldn't function without Kaley&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:18.900
Cuoco as Penny. Penny was initially designed&nbsp;
to be a foil to Leonard and Sheldon when Chuck&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:23.460
Lorre presented the show's pilot to several&nbsp;
networks. However, that plan changed after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:27.600
test audiences and TV executives were&nbsp;
unimpressed with that version of Penny.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:28.380
"…Molecules."

00:00:29.034 --> 00:00:33.360
As devoted fans may already be aware, the&nbsp;
first iteration wasn't even named Penny;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:38.520
she was named Katie, and she was not played by&nbsp;
Kaley Cuoco. That first incarnation was dark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:42.780
and interestingly, Marisa Tomei was one&nbsp;
of the leading candidates for the role.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:47.280
Jim Parsons acknowledged just how different the&nbsp;
show would have been while talking with People&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.900
Magazine and it's difficult to disagree.&nbsp;
The dynamic between Sheldon and Penny is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:55.740
undoubtedly one of the show's highlights, and&nbsp;
it's difficult to imagine a version in which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.740 --> 00:01:00.960
Penny isn't a bubbly and understanding delight&nbsp;
who challenges Sheldon's dislike of humanity.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:04.740
By now many viewers know that&nbsp;
the actors who played Leonard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:08.400
and Penny were also romantically&nbsp;
involved. In the book, Kaley Cuoco&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.880
revealed that this mutual attraction&nbsp;
began pretty quickly. She mentioned,

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.880
But, of course, both were in different&nbsp;
relationships when their attraction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:22.320
began. Still, it became real when Johnny&nbsp;
Galecki invited Cuoco on a wine date,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:24.360
and the rest, as they say, is history.

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:29.460
For a long time, the two managed to keep their&nbsp;
relationship hidden from not only the media, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:34.200
also the rest of the cast and crew of the show.&nbsp;
However, the sneaking around ultimately led them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:39.030
to decide to reveal their relationship to creator&nbsp;
Chuck Lorre at Comic-Con, who said in the book -

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:56.160
Sheldon's relationships are a major source&nbsp;
of comedy in the series. He does not like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:59.700
other people. He even hilariously&nbsp;
categorizes his pals; Leonard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:03.900
Penny, and Raj are his best friends, whereas&nbsp;
Howard is only a "treasured acquaintance."

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:08.880
And when he is interested in someone, such as&nbsp;
Leonard's mother, it is typically not romantic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:12.420
Furthermore, Sheldon's romantic&nbsp;
exploits are frequently one-sided,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:17.160
whether it's his one-time date with Lalita or&nbsp;
his awkward platonic connection with Ramona.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:21.810
According to the book, Chuck Lorre initially&nbsp;
pushed for Sheldon to be asexual, saying -

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:37.680
An asexual Sheldon would've been interesting,&nbsp;
given that sort of depiction in pop culture is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:42.840
uncommon. On the other hand, the writers chose to&nbsp;
make Sheldon meet his match in Amy. In some ways,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:46.620
this works better for the show since it gives&nbsp;
Sheldon's character arc a sense of growth.

00:02:46.996 --> 00:02:50.460
Leonard and Penny's romance finally&nbsp;
takes off at the start of the third&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:52.500
season. When they eventually start dating, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.601
things come to a standstill when Leonard tells&nbsp;
Penny he loves her, and she can't say it back.

00:02:56.601 --> 00:03:00.251
"Ah, the premature I love you."

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:03.000
In the book, co-creator Bill Prady stated that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:06.420
Cuoco confided in him that the writing&nbsp;
on the show accurately captured what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:10.470
Galecki and Cuoco experienced during&nbsp;
their separation, with Prady saying -

00:03:16.232 --> 00:03:18.180
Unlike their on-screen counterparts, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:23.266
Galecki and Cuoco never reunited. However,&nbsp;
both pairs ended up in good situations.

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:28.800
Howard Wolowitz is the show's closest thing to a&nbsp;
villain. That's not because he's a horrible guy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:33.720
but because he needs to grow the most out of the&nbsp;
bunch. He is frequently creepy with ladies and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:37.500
makes incredibly inappropriate remarks&nbsp;
about his closest friend Raj. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:41.580
as the series progresses, the introduction&nbsp;
of Bernadette and the exploration of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:46.320
relationship with his mother reveal another&nbsp;
side of him. The character's intricacy keeps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:50.160
him compelling throughout the show. And it's all&nbsp;
held together by Simon Helberg's performance.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:55.620
In another reality, though, Simon Helberg did&nbsp;
not play Howard Wolowitz. Kevin Sussman was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:59.700
the first choice for the role, but he couldn't&nbsp;
take it due to a contractual obligation with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:03.240
"Ugly Betty." According to Entertainment&nbsp;
Tonight, this revelation even shocked the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:07.080
author Jessica Radloff, and she was&nbsp;
initially hesitant to tell Helberg.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:12.000
Of course, Sussman ended up playing Stuart Bloom,&nbsp;
the owner of the comic book store frequented by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.660
the gang. Radloff praised Sussman for&nbsp;
never bringing up the fact that he was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:18.840
the first choice for Howard throughout&nbsp;
the entire show's production, adding -

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:27.000
Raj is first introduced to fans as the gang's&nbsp;
pal who can't talk to women while sober. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:31.560
he drinks, he has the confidence to speak to&nbsp;
women ... but can only do so in an offensive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:35.640
manner. Kunal Nayyar generally performed&nbsp;
the character lightheartedly, and he always&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:39.960
had a fantastic sense of humor with the show's&nbsp;
writing, despite usually being the butt of jokes.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:44.700
So Jessica Radloff's revelation that CBS&nbsp;
initially chose to go behind Chuck Lorre's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:48.960
back in order to replace Nayyar came as&nbsp;
a great surprise, with Lorre saying -

00:04:56.700 --> 00:05:01.500
Lorre immediately went to CBS executives to&nbsp;
express his unhappiness at being belittled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:05.400
and to make it clear that he would not allow&nbsp;
Nayyar to depart the show without a fight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:10.338
Since then, Raj has joined the pantheon of&nbsp;
brilliant television supporting characters.

00:05:10.453 --> 00:05:11.621
"Later losers!"

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:15.420
"The Big Bang Theory" became a pop-cultural giant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:19.440
and for sitcoms, that generally means big&nbsp;
stars making appearances on the show. "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:23.400
Office" went from a first season with no major&nbsp;
celebrities to having guest stars like James&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:27.540
Spader and Idris Elba in the later seasons.&nbsp;
It goes without saying celebrity cameos on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:31.500
"The Big Bang Theory" became commonplace,&nbsp;
but they didn't always pan out as intended.

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:36.360
Selena Gomez was one of the stars who never&nbsp;
made it to the show. In Jessica Radloff's book,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:40.860
Steven Molaro, one of the show's producers, talked&nbsp;
about the moment Selena Gomez shared a social&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:45.480
media photo of herself watching the show. Molaro&nbsp;
then reached out to her team to see if they could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:49.860
plan a guest star spot for Gomez, but her hectic&nbsp;
schedule prevented her from appearing on the show.

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:53.700
Although Molaro never made it to the&nbsp;
pitching stage, he did reveal that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:57.840
writers were contemplating having Gomez play&nbsp;
Amy's stepsister. The idea was to make Amy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:03.435
slightly irritated with Gomez's character and&nbsp;
envious of her since, well, she's Selena Gomez.

00:06:03.435 --> 00:06:06.060
Penny is presented in "The Big Bang Theory"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:10.500
as having an active and sporting lifestyle.&nbsp;
Her father wanted a boy, so when he got Penny,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:14.880
he raised her just like he would a son. As a&nbsp;
result, Penny is good with engines, enjoys sports,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:19.740
and once stole a horse while intoxicated in high&nbsp;
school. In that particular regard, her real-life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:24.720
counterpart, Kaley Cuoco, is no different.&nbsp;
Cuoco is well renowned for her love of horses.

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:29.520
However, the only problem with an active lifestyle&nbsp;
is sometimes it leads to terrifying injuries.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:34.320
Cuoco experienced this during a horse-riding&nbsp;
accident. In the book Chuck Lorre and Cuoco&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:39.000
reminisced about a horse-riding accident that&nbsp;
almost led to her leg's amputation. According&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:43.440
to People Magazine, Cuoco fell from her horse in&nbsp;
2010 because the horse was startled by something,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:46.800
and while she was on the ground,&nbsp;
the animal trod on her left leg.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:51.840
Cuoco, thankfully, did not lose her leg.&nbsp;
Nonetheless, the anxiety was valid and spread&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:55.860
among the cast and crew. While Cuoco later&nbsp;
remarked that the experience was still too&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.860 --> 00:07:00.840
new and horrific for her to relive fully, she was&nbsp;
back on her feet in a matter of weeks. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:05.400
despite her injuries, she returned to work, but&nbsp;
the writers made her a bartender so that she could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:09.960
hide her cast and she needed to employ a body&nbsp;
double in circumstances when Penny needed to walk.

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:14.700
Mark Hamill is, without a doubt, one&nbsp;
of the most influential actors of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:18.360
generation. In geek culture, though, his&nbsp;
work in "Star Wars" movies and "Batman:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:23.340
The Animated Series" has made him a virtual&nbsp;
deity. So it's no surprise that Hamill was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:27.768
considered for a guest appearance on the show and&nbsp;
luckily, his schedule permitted him to stop by.

00:07:27.864 --> 00:07:29.496
"Congratulations on your wedding."

00:07:29.935 --> 00:07:34.639
"Thank you. When this is over I&nbsp;
have 4,000 things for you to sign."

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:39.120
However, while Hamill agreed to appear on the&nbsp;
show, he had only seen a couple of episodes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:43.830
and had no idea how important the show was to&nbsp;
pop culture at the time, saying in the book -

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:01.260
Hamill admitted that his appearance&nbsp;
and subsequent viewing of the entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:04.260
show made him regret his approach&nbsp;
to the performance, conceding -

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:12.540
It's no secret that the first season of "The&nbsp;
Big Bang Theory" is centered around Leonard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:17.460
and Penny's romance, with Sheldon serving as a&nbsp;
quirky friend who balances the drama with humor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:22.320
But as the series progressed, the audience grew&nbsp;
to adore Sheldon and got invested in seeing him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:26.520
overcome his struggles, especially in terms&nbsp;
of how he interacts with others. So in a way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:29.880
the show became an ensemble piece&nbsp;
with Sheldon at its heart. That was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:32.940
due in large part to Jim Parsons'&nbsp;
endearing performance in the role.

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:37.560
However, after 12 seasons, Parsons thought it&nbsp;
was time to let go and move on with his career.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:42.360
Parsons proposed to Lorre that he depart the&nbsp;
show and they all carry on without him. The only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:47.220
problem was that none of the other cast members&nbsp;
were aware of Parsons' feelings. Galecki stated -

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:56.940
The cast and crew decided against continuing&nbsp;
the show without him since they thought it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.940 --> 00:09:00.600
wouldn't work if one of the cast members&nbsp;
left. So, after expressing their feelings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:04.777
they all agreed to end the show after&nbsp;
Parsons voiced his intention to leave.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:09.300
Later in the show's existence, the emphasis&nbsp;
moves to Sheldon's growth and struggles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:13.260
especially with his dislike of the human&nbsp;
touch. One way the sitcom portrays this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:17.040
is through Penny's friendship with Sheldon. It&nbsp;
begins with them aggravating each other a lot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:21.720
but the audience gradually realizes how precious&nbsp;
their friendship is. Penny looks after Sheldon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:25.380
when he is unwell, and Sheldon returns the&nbsp;
favor when Penny dislocates her shoulder.

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:29.400
Sheldon's journey and friendship with&nbsp;
Penny climaxes with an uncharacteristic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:34.620
hug initiated by Sheldon. Even though the hug is&nbsp;
out of character, it's well-planned and earned.

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:37.380
"Leonard look, Sheldon's hugging me!"

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:41.580
"It's a Saturnalia miracle!"

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:43.980
In the book, Parsons explained -

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:58.080
Parsons was referring to the Christmas&nbsp;
episode in which Penny gives him a napkin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:03.000
used and signed by Leonard Nimoy. Sheldon&nbsp;
is overwhelmed with gratitude and reasons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:06.060
that the only way he can repay&nbsp;
her generosity is to hug her.

